        "### Naïve Bayes Implementation\n",
        "\n",
        "This section demonstrates the implementation of the Naïve Bayes algorithm using `scikit-learn`. We will cover:\n",
        "1.  Generating a synthetic dataset.\n",
        "2.  Splitting the dataset into training and testing sets.\n",
        "3.  Training a Gaussian Naïve Bayes classifier.\n",
        "4.  Making predictions.\n",
        "5.  Evaluating the model using a confusion matrix and accuracy score."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e60ab573"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Import necessary libraries\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.naive_bayes import GaussianNB\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, accuracy_score\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns"
      ],
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": []
    },
