      "metadata": {
        "id": "62372b9d"
      },
      "source": [
        "#### 1. Generate a Synthetic Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "For demonstration purposes, let's create a simple classification dataset. We'll use `make_classification` from `sklearn.datasets` to generate features (X) and target labels (y)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 223
        },
        "id": "c6ec701e",
        "outputId": "3c737610-87ea-4be9-c504-eb6a841b8845"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate a synthetic dataset\n",
        "X, y = make_classification(n_samples=200, n_features=2, n_informative=2,\n",
        "                           n_redundant=0, n_clusters_per_class=1,\n",
        "                           random_state=42, class_sep=1.5)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to DataFrame for easier viewing (optional)\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(X, columns=['feature_1', 'feature_2'])\n",
        "df['target'] = y\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"First 5 rows of the dataset:\")\n",
        "display(df.head())"
